from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,re,subprocess,datetime
L=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];R=json.loads((L/'outputs/records.json').read_text());reserved=json.loads((L/'reservation.json').read_text())
h=lambda b:hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()
D={
350971:('parked','primary conjecture and adjacent proposition review; three versions','Conjecture 2.1 (v3); Conjecture 2.2 (v1,v2)','Open-convex embedding dimension 2 versus arbitrary convex embedding dimension 1. The source proves only classes satisfying Proposition 2.1 and gives a counterexample to the converse. Those examples do not refute this record.','No computational coverage. Need either a mixed-interval code with a proved open planar realization and proved absence of open interval realizations, or a full interval-regularization theorem under open convexity. Arbitrary interval endpoint failures alone are ineligible.'),
350974:('parked','primary conjecture, orbit-bound proof context, finite family computation','Conjecture 5.4 in arXiv v1; journal Conjecture 5.6','The 2n/3 regular-orbit bound is stronger than the source theorem. Complete small-family automorphism enumeration produced no eligible violation. The K3,3 exception fails as expected.','orbits.json: all automorphisms of prisms C_h square K_2 and Mobius ladders on 2h vertices, 3 <= h <= 15. This is 26 specified families, not a census. Need a nonexceptional cubic vertex-transitive graph and automorphism below 2n/3, or a global orbit-count argument.'),
351019:('parked','primary statement and adjacent theorem review; two versions','Conjecture 4.2','Freest matroid maximality is universal over all matroids with the specified circuits. The source proves bipartite representation comparisons and moment-curve coincidences, which do not settle maximality.','No exhaustive matroid search. Need a certified competing matroid freer on a specific set, or a full maximality proof. Generic rigidity rank examples alone do not refute it; high Lean semantic cost.'),
351089:('excluded_known_source_theorem','primary theorem and proof read; two versions','Proposition 2.16, deduced from Theorem 2.15(2)','The source itself proves precisely the Hurwitz stability claim after stating Conjecture 2.13. Substitution alpha=2n, beta=1, gamma=0, mu=-1, phi=1, mn=2n-1 gives its proposition.','No search warranted; no new endpoint.'),
351097:('parked','primary gonality statement and source computation scope; two versions','Conjecture 1.1; source companion gonality/discrete-vs-metric-dgon','The source refutes subdivision invariance, not the reserved Brill-Noether gonality bound. The authors tested every simple graph through 13 vertices (about 8000 CPU hours). Metric gonality cannot be substituted for divisorial gonality.','No duplicate small sweep. Need a genuinely discrete divisor certificate on a multigraph beyond known scope or a full theorem; no clear bounded route survived.'),
351235:('parked','primary definition/theorem/conjecture bodies; arXiv and journal','Conjecture 2.4; Theorem 2.3','The sufficiency direction is already Theorem 2.3. A finite iteration reaching a size cap is not proof of divergence, and does not prove the necessity claim false.','purepn.json covers connected labeled simple graphs through 6 vertices with at most v+2 edges, path orders 4 through v, up to 10 iterations subject to 15-vertex/22-edge caps. Need an invariant infinite divergent orbit avoiding every long-cycle obstruction, or a necessity theorem.'),
351237:('parked','primary minimality lemmas and conjecture; arXiv and journal; exact bounded graph diagnostics','Conjecture 3.5; Lemmas 3.2-3.4; Theorem 3.11','No non-unicyclic convergent graph survived the edge-deletion necessary minimality screen in the completed small search. Full minimality was not inferred from that screen. Source excludes terminating sequences from convergence.','purepn.json and logs/purepn.log. Need a convergent graph with no convergent proper subgraph and a non-unicyclic component; or remove the source girth hypothesis with a full proof.'),
351238:('parked','primary exact uniqueness scope and source figures; arXiv and journal','Conjecture 3.12; Figure 10; Conjecture 2.9','Uniqueness is the new part; existence follows from finite subgraph minimalization. Two isomorphic embeddings or a disconnected union do not provide a substantive new refutation.','The same bounded orbit computation was relevant but did not enumerate all minimal subgraphs or certify uniqueness. Need two genuinely distinct minimal convergent subgraphs in an eligible convergent graph, after comparison with Figure 10.'),
351278:('parked','primary conjecture, spectral hypotheses and proof ingredients; two versions','Conjecture 1; main theorem for eigenvalues >= -2','The source proves the conjecture under a lower spectral bound, rather than for all finite groups. Published k=3 and regular-complement restrictions are partial. An arbitrary regular graph is not a character-degree graph.','No group table enumeration; no GAP dependency installed. Need an explicit finite group with certified irreducible character degrees outside the two graph families or a full structural proof.'),
351502:('parked','primary definition, Theorem 2.9 and Conjecture 2.10 review','Conjecture 2.10','The two stated packing cases are the source remaining cases for intersecting linear Ryser. Low-r cases already have classical coverage; an arbitrary intersecting hypergraph without a certified r-partition would be irrelevant.','No exhaustive hypergraph search; famous full-scope problem, no finite tractable route identified. Need a multipartite linear intersecting system violating Ryser with exact transversal and packing certificates.'),
351573:('excluded_known_source_theorem','primary Theorem 3.4 and full short proof read','Theorem 3.4','The source proves the exact all-even-n-not-power-of-two claim. Write n=2^a k with k odd, use the existing degree-2k group and a regular group of degree 2^(a-1), then Corollary 3.3 yields n/2 parts.','No new search or Lean endpoint warranted.'),
351595:('excluded_known_source_theorem','primary Theorem 3 and proof read','Theorem 3, Section 4','The source proves the exact k + sum(t_i-1) bound stated as Conjecture 1 in its introduction, using Lemmas 5-6 and simultaneous cotree diagonalization.','No new search or Lean endpoint warranted.'),
351703:('excluded_prior_2026_resolution','primary source Theorem 46 and 2026 follow-up Theorem 34/proof read; finite Walsh diagnostics','Ahmadi-Shafaeiabr Theorem 46; Wang et al., arXiv:2609.37093, Theorem 34','Source covers classes (c)-(k). September 2026 follow-up explicitly proves (a),(b) and hence all eleven classes, including dual distance. This independently excludes novelty.','codes.json and codes-extended.json: all eleven trinomials for every odd m=5,7,...,19; exact additive Walsh distributions all match. Diagnostics do not prove all m and do not earn credit. Follow-up source body saved.'),
351718:('parked','primary density definitions, source table and Section 3.20; three versions','Section 3.20, unnumbered lower-bound sharpness conjecture','These four parameters are asymptotic densities despite finite-cue routing. Finite counts alone cannot refute a limiting density. The nearby K5-equals refutation found online concerns a different forbidden graph and is not this record.','No finite exhaustive hypergraph search. Need an asymptotically valid new forbidden-graph-free construction beating one bound, with a proved density, or all four upper bounds. High proof cost; no scope substitution.'),
351926:('parked','primary Definition 7.3.1, Conjecture 7.3.2 and surrounding discussion read','Conjecture 7.3.2','This is elimination-rule admissibility in an unbounded proof calculus. Failure to find a CS derivation at a finite depth cannot refute existence of some k prime.','No bounded search presented as a disproof. Need a syntactic invariant separating the calculi or a complete simulation theorem for nontrivial eliminated subexpressions.'),
352005:('parked','primary exact even-set scope; source versions; 2026 citing paper body; heuristic and reduced exhaustive diagnostics','O Neill Conjecture 1; Han-Zhang-Zhao arXiv:2608.16321 Theorem 1.2','Recent work proves the bound through a fixed positive fraction of 2^floor(n/2), not full stated range. No violation found. Source-formula equality constructions are known and receive no credit.','eventown.json: n=6,8,10,12, three excess choices each, 8 restarts of 12000 proposals before used-vector rejection. eventown-exact.json: n=6 all s=3,4,5,6 via twin-class reduction; minima 12,16,20,24. Need a global lower bound or an independently certified violation beyond known constructions.'),
352066:('parked','primary signed-girth class and conjecture discussion; citing-work search','Conjecture 3.6; class P_k star','The ordinary and signed planar circular-colouring settings must be kept distinct. Nonplanar counterexamples to Jaeger circular flow do not refute the planar target. The source table contains only partial bounds.','No signed-planar enumeration implemented. Need exact membership in P_(4p+1) star and a circular-colouring obstruction, including signed walk girth semantics; no concrete small route survived.'),
352083:('excluded_source_construction','primary circuit relation, all four source versions, Example 21; exact rank comparison','Definition 52 and Conjecture 56 in arXiv v4; journal Definition 50 and Conjecture 54','Both a loop-coloop extension and a loopless/cocolopless finite diagnostic fail transitivity in M and its dual. The stronger diagnostic is EXACTLY isomorphic to the second matrix of printed Example 21. It is therefore a source-construction counterexample, expressly ineligible.','q-source-isomorphism.json checks all 67 subspaces of F2^4 under basis images (1,12,4,3). Search stopped once subsumption was proved. No Lean endpoint promoted; no novel candidate.'),
352440:('parked','primary thesis scope and complexity conjecture; 2022 follow-up search','Conjecture 6.21','Parameters count given horizontal and vertical lines. The MathDB paraphrase obscures that general input scope. Polynomial APUD(1,1) recognition is a special case and does not settle general NP membership or contradict NP-completeness with parameters in the input.','No numerical route can establish NP membership. Need polynomial-size representation certificates or a complexity classification; source NP-hardness is already known.'),
352484:('parked','primary initial-position conjecture and preceding strategy discussion','Conjecture 2.27','Infinite Hex here uses an infinite winning path condition. Finite-board wins, arbitrarily long finite prongs, and failure of a pairing strategy do not prove a Red win.','No finite-board search claimed relevant. Need a genuine infinite winning strategy under exact directional path rules, or a Blue drawing strategy. High semantic Lean cost.')}
results={}
for i in reserved['ids']:
 v=R[str(i)];r=v['record'];a=r['source_url'].split('/')[-1];outcome,depth,label,reason,attempt=D[i]
 receipts=[]
 for p in sorted((L/'sources').glob(a+'*.receipt.json')):
  receipts.append({'path':str(p.relative_to(L)),'sha256':h(p.read_bytes()),'receipt':json.loads(p.read_text())})
 results[str(i)]={'mathdb_id':i,'title':r['title'],'outcome':outcome,'credit':0,'review_depth':depth,'source_locator':label,'literal_statement':r['statement'],'statement_sha256':h(r['statement'].encode()),'provenance':{k:v[k] for k in ['chunk','line','chunk_sha256','raw_sha256']},'raw_file':f'outputs/{i}.raw.jsonl','source_url':r['source_url'],'source_receipts':receipts,'reason':reason,'attempts_and_remaining_gap':attempt,'lean_endpoint':None,'novelty_clearance':False,'registry_evidence':['outputs/registry-screen.json','outputs/registry-complete-supplement.json','outputs/registry-final-supplement.json'],'history_screen':'outputs/historical-id-screen.txt','limitations':['No worldwide priority claim. Parked is not a resolution. Finite computations are diagnostics without Lean semantics. Full citation closure and full upstream proof audit were not performed.']}
(L/'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
# Preserve source example/figure inventory, rather than selecting only a favourable obstruction.
inv={}
for p in sorted((L/'sources').glob('*.txt')):
 if p.name.startswith(('2107.03905','carbonero-journal','2109.13637','2108.10042')):
  inv[p.name]=[{'line':n,'text':s} for n,s in enumerate(p.read_text(errors='replace').splitlines(),1) if re.search(r'Example \d|Figure \d|Fig\. \d',s)]
(L/'outputs/printed-example-inventory.json').write_text(json.dumps(inv,indent=2))
patterns=['Franke','Muthiah','regular.orbit','hyperconnectivity','alternating.run polynomial','minimal.*convergent','Tong.Viet','common Laplacian','tri.weight','elementary entailment','eventown','q.matroid','Infinite Hex','APUD']
r=subprocess.run(['rg','-n','-i','|'.join(patterns),str(L.parent),'-g','SUMMARY.md','-g','CANDIDATE.md'],capture_output=True,text=True)
lines=[s for s in r.stdout.splitlines() if str(L) not in s];(L/'outputs/historical-title-screen.txt').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
# Resource/log/source manifest. Never mutate receipts.
manifest={}
for folder in ['sources','logs','outputs']:
 for p in sorted((L/folder).iterdir()):
  if p.is_file():manifest[str(p.relative_to(L))]={'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':h(p.read_bytes())}
(L/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
assert len(results)==20 and set(map(int,results))==set(reserved['ids'])
print('20 entries;',sum(x['outcome'].startswith('excluded') for x in results.values()),'excluded;',sum(x['outcome']=='parked' for x in results.values()),'parked')
